{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789396508,"nonce":"1wibLgLiVAIJOLFxFvETGcDC81I=","title":"Live register files leak across fiber stacks","message":"live_regs kept one thread-local stack of register-file pointers and\npopped on guard drop, assuming activations nest on one stack. Under\nkrio backing an interpreter activation on a fiber's stack registers,\nthe fiber yields, the host's own activations push and pop underneath\nit, and the pops unwind the wrong entries; a fiber dropped while\nsuspended never runs its guards at all (krio unmaps the stack without\nunwinding), so its pointer stayed registered and the next collection\nread through it. hatch/site under WLIFT_KRIO_FIBER=1 WLIFT_GC_STRESS=1\ndied in collect_live_values after ~100 requests.\n\nEach entry now records the fiber stack it was made on; a guard removes\nits own entry wherever it sits, and KrioStack::drop forgets every entry\nof its stack before the seam is told.","files":null}]}